"Lift grows quickly with speed. If a plane goes twice as fast, its wings make four times as much lift. That is why a plane races down the runway: it must go fast enough for the lift to be bigger than its weight. Tilting the wing up a little more gives more lift too, but only up to a point. If the angle gets too steep, the air can no longer follow the top of the wing, and the lift suddenly drops. This is called a stall.": "c3d912948cca",
